                {"question": "What happens when copy ignores a reader's unspoken objections?", "options": ["Nothing, objections don't affect conversion", "The copy tends to lose the sale silently, without complaint", "The reader always asks for clarification", "It has no effect on persuasion"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "Readers with unaddressed doubts simply leave without acting, rather than voicing their objection — so copy must anticipate and answer it."},
                {"question": "What is one effective way to defuse the objection 'this is too expensive'?", "options": ["Ignoring the price entirely", "Offering a free trial or a concrete value comparison", "Removing the price from the page", "Making the CTA button bigger"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "A free trial or clear value comparison structurally reduces the perceived risk or cost objection."},
                {"question": "What tone should copy use when addressing a reader's skepticism?", "options": ["Defensive and argumentative", "Calm acknowledgment followed by a direct answer", "Ignoring the doubt completely", "Aggressive dismissal of the concern"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "Calmly acknowledging the doubt before answering it builds trust, whereas a defensive tone can increase skepticism."}
